                        "entry_id": "7690a63d-071a-316e-a06e-c00e12114f88",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "urnae"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6210bc6f-df05-34e6-9f0c-4baf21c0005b",
                        "entry_id": "7690a63d-071a-316e-a06e-c00e12114f88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Roman unit of liquid measure reckoned as the volume of 40 Roman pounds of wine and equivalent to about 13 L although differing slightly over time."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed40f6ef-d55f-4be1-9bdf-d90a9910c54d",
                                "sense_id": "6210bc6f-df05-34e6-9f0c-4baf21c0005b",
                                "text": "A wine vessel, probably the Roman urna, which contained half the quantity of the amphora."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec272378-a41f-486c-9bf4-17648183e958",
                                "sense_id": "6210bc6f-df05-34e6-9f0c-4baf21c0005b",
                                "text": "The congius was the 8th part of the amphora, and the 4th of the urna: it contained 6 sextarii."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "546ed71b-3d3a-41bb-882c-08c671f3f6ee",
                                "sense_id": "6210bc6f-df05-34e6-9f0c-4baf21c0005b",
                                "text": "It follows that the seah must equal the urna, and the hin equal 2 Attic choes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
